@startuml backend_recovery
title Existing O3 recovery sources and the new IBPU feedback boundary
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

participant "IEW" as IEW
participant "iewQueue / IEWStruct" as IQ
participant "Commit / ROB" as Commit
participant "timeBuffer / TimeStruct" as TB
participant "Decode" as Decode
participant "Fetch" as Fetch
participant "BAC" as BAC
participant "Gem5BpuBridge" as Bridge
participant "FTQ + BlockFetchEngine" as Frontend
participant "IBPU" as BPU

legend left
  [E] Existing gem5 method or signal
  [N] Proposed IBPU / bridge integration
  [A] Illustrative internal operation, not an existing method
  Signal arrows are delayed delivery, not direct C++ calls.
endlegend

== Execute discovers an actual misprediction ==
IEW -> IEW : [E] executeInsts(): inst->mispredicted()
IEW -> IEW : [E] squashDueToBranch(inst, tid)
IEW -> IQ : [E] squash=true; squashedSeqNum=inst->seqNum\n\
includeSquashInst=false; mispredictInst=inst\nbranchTaken; pc=actual next PC
note right of IEW
  IEW keeps the oldest squash request it has seen.
  Memory-order violations use includeSquashInst=true.
  Source: iew.cc:473, 497, 1279.
end note
... iewToCommitDelay via iewQueue ...
IQ --> Commit : [E] fromIEW squash fields
Commit -> Commit : [E] commit(): arbitrate with traps / TC / squash-after\n\
check squashedSeqNum <= youngestSeqNum
Commit -> Commit : [E] rob->squash(cut, tid)
Commit -> TB : [E] commitInfo: squash=true; doneSeqNum=cut\n\
robSquashing=true; pc; mispredictInst; branchTaken
note right of Commit
  Source: commit.cc:755-846; comm.hh:TimeStruct::CommitComm.
  The same doneSeqNum field means a squash boundary here;
  it does NOT announce retirement of that instruction.
end note
... configured stage delays; BAC runs before Fetch in CPU::tick() ...
TB --> BAC : [E] fromCommit after commitToFetchDelay
BAC -> BAC : [E] checkAndUpdateBPUSignals(tid): commit squash first
BAC -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer)
Bridge -> Frontend : [N] invalidate affected payloads, slices and requests
Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(cause=Execute / Trap / Other, cut, \
restartPC,\nresolvedOutcome only for an executed control instruction)
BPU -> BPU : [A] restore speculative history; discard younger tokens\n\
retain corrected surviving branch until retirement
note over BAC, BPU
  IBPU mode replaces legacy squashBpuHistories()/bpu->squash().
  Keep the existing BAC PC/status/FTQ recovery responsibilities.
  Never call both history owners for the same prediction.
  Existing route: bac.cc:290-330; squash():484.
end note
TB --> Fetch : [E] commitInfo.squash after commitToFetchDelay
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] squashFromCommit() -> doSquash()\n\
reset PC/decoder/requests; clear local fetchQueue
Fetch -> Frontend : [N] cancel affected assembly; reject canceled completions
note over Commit, Fetch
  Decode / Rename / IEW also consume the existing commit broadcast
  after their configured delays. ROB, IQ, LSQ and rename recovery
  stay on the existing O3 path; they do not call IBPU directly.
  Fetch also removes instructions not in ROB (fetch.cc:698).
end note

== Decode discovers a wrong direct target earlier ==
Decode -> Decode : [E] decodeInsts(): direct control,\n\
unconditional or predicted taken, target != readPredTarg()
Decode -> Decode : [E] squash(inst, false, tid)
Decode -> TB : [E] decodeInfo: squash=true; doneSeqNum=inst->seqNum\n\
nextPC=branchTarget(); branchTaken; mispredictInst
Decode -> Decode : [E] clear younger decode state; removeInstsUntil(seq, \
tid)\nsetPredTarg(correct direct target)
... decodeToFetchDelay ...
TB --> BAC : [E] fromDecode->decodeInfo
BAC -> BAC : [E] commit squash? return\n\
else commit doneSeqNum? update first\nthen process decode squash and return
BAC -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer)
Bridge -> Frontend : [N] invalidate affected frontend suffix
Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(cause=Decode, cut, restartPC,\n\
resolvedOutcome absent unless fully known)
BPU -> BPU : [A] repair direct-target metadata and speculative history
TB --> Fetch : [E] decodeInfo.squash (unless already Squashing)
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] squashFromDecode() -> doSquash()\n\
removeInstsUntil(seq, tid)
Fetch -> Frontend : [N] cancel affected assembly and requests
note over Decode, BPU
  Direct-target information is known at decode; the direction of
  a conditional branch still needs execution. Preserve that distinction.
  CFI.isPrediction=false alone does not prove execution resolution.
  Unexpected non-control predicted taken currently panics; the code
  below that panic is not a working recovery path.
  Sources: decode.cc:311, 705-741; bac.cc:331-359;
  fetch.cc:685, 950; comm.hh:TimeStruct::DecodeComm.
end note

== Fetch requests a BAC resteer ==
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] fetch(): current PC outside FT range\n\
or updatePC/predecode requests repair
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] bacResteer(newPC, tid)
Fetch -> TB : [E] fetchInfo.squash=true; nextPC=newPC
Fetch -> Frontend : [E] ftq->invalidate(tid)
Fetch -> Bridge : [N] retain exact repair boundary from binding/cursor
note right of Bridge
  Existing FetchComm carries only squash and nextPC.
  Multi-block recovery needs a sidecar RecoveryPoint or a small
  FetchComm extension: key/block/CFI/instSeq, not just the PC.
end note
... fetchToBacDelay ...
TB --> BAC : [E] fromFetch->fetchInfo
BAC -> BAC : [E] check only after commit/decode processing\n\
and only when bacStatus != Squashing
BAC -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer)
Bridge -> Frontend : [N] discard bad suffix; preserve valid consumed bindings
Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(cause=FetchRepair, cut, restartPC,\n\
resolvedOutcome absent)
note over Fetch, BPU
  bacResteer is Fetch -> BAC, not a BPU -> backend redirect hook.
  Sources: fetch.cc:762, 1102, 1377; bac.cc:361-370.
  Wiring/delays: bac.cc:120-122; fetch.cc:250-253.
end note
@enduml
